Only 4 custom metrics exist across the entire codebase. No visibility into command/query throughput, error rates, or latency — the most important operational signals.

Implement a Wolverine middleware (not MediatR behavior — Foundry uses Wolverine) that automatically instruments ALL command and query handlers:

```csharp
public sealed class TelemetryMiddleware
{
    private static readonly Meter _meter = Diagnostics.CreateMeter("Application");
    private static readonly Counter<long> _commandsExecuted = _meter.CreateCounter<long>("foundry.commands.executed_total");
    private static readonly Counter<long> _commandsFailed = _meter.CreateCounter<long>("foundry.commands.failed_total");
    private static readonly Histogram<double> _commandDuration = _meter.CreateHistogram<double>("foundry.commands.duration_seconds");

    public static async Task<T> BeforeAsync<T>(Envelope envelope, ILogger logger)
    {
        // start stopwatch, set tags
    }
    public static void Finally(Envelope envelope, Stopwatch sw)
    {
        TagList tags = new()
        {
            { "command.type", envelope.MessageType },
            { "module", ExtractModule(envelope) },
        };
        _commandsExecuted.Add(1, tags);
        _commandDuration.Record(sw.Elapsed.TotalSeconds, tags);
    }
}
```

Register the middleware in Wolverine options. This single middleware covers ALL modules with zero per-module work.

Also add the meter name to the OTel metrics config: .AddMeter("Foundry.Application")

BUG: In ConversationsController.cs:73, InvoicesController.cs:117, PaymentsController.cs:96, and SubscriptionsController.cs:96, result.Value is accessed to build the URL string BEFORE ToCreatedResult checks IsSuccess. If the result is a failure, this throws InvalidOperationException('Cannot access value of a failed result') which hits GlobalExceptionHandler as a 500 instead of the correct error response.

Pattern to fix:
```csharp
// BROKEN - result.Value accessed unconditionally
Result<Guid> result = await _bus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command, ct);
return result.ToCreatedResult($"/api/v1/resource/{result.Value}");

// FIX - check success first, or pass a URL factory
if (!result.IsSuccess) return result.ToActionResult();
return Results.Created($"/api/v1/resource/{result.Value}", result.Value);
// OR add a ToCreatedResult overload that takes a Func<T, string> urlFactory
```

