## Vulnerability (NEW-IDENT-001, HIGH, Risk Score 16)

GetUsers() at UsersController.cs:43-51 calls _keycloakAdmin.GetUsersAsync(search, first, max, ct) which queries ALL Keycloak realm users without tenant/organization filtering. Compare with GetUserById() which validates UserBelongsToTenantAsync().

**Attack Scenario:** Any user with UsersRead permission lists all users across all tenants, exposing usernames, emails, and user IDs.

## Files to Modify
- src/Modules/Identity/Foundry.Identity.Api/Controllers/UsersController.cs

## Remediation
Replace the GetUsers implementation to use the organization members endpoint:
```csharp
[HttpGet]
[HasPermission(PermissionType.UsersRead)]
public async Task<ActionResult<PagedResult<UserDto>>> GetUsers(
    [FromQuery] string? search, [FromQuery] int first = 0,
    [FromQuery] int max = 50, CancellationToken ct = default)
{
    IReadOnlyList<UserDto> orgMembers = await _keycloakOrg
        .GetMembersAsync(_tenantContext.TenantId.Value, ct);
    IEnumerable<UserDto> filtered = orgMembers;
    if (\!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(search))
    {
        filtered = orgMembers.Where(u =>
            u.Email.Contains(search, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ||
            u.FirstName.Contains(search, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ||
            u.LastName.Contains(search, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
    }
    List<UserDto> paged = filtered.Skip(first).Take(max).ToList();
    return Ok(new PagedResult<UserDto>(paged, orgMembers.Count));
}
```

## Testing
- Verify GetUsers returns only users from current tenant's organization
- Verify search filtering works within tenant-scoped results
- Verify pagination works correctly
- Verify cross-tenant users are NOT returned

HIGH (Risk 20). UsersController DeactivateUser, ActivateUser, AssignRole, RemoveRole (lines 115-157) lack the organization membership check that GetUserById has (lines 66-72). Cross-tenant IDOR vulnerability.

