Migrate all three React apps (apps/examples/minimal-app, apps/wallow-auth, apps/wallow-web) to real TanStack Start applications, app by app, then delete the hand-rolled SSR platform (packages/web-shell's server layer) and sweep stale hosting docs/comments.

Shared config shape across all three apps -- CORRECTED by the 4.1 spike (see the PLAN CORRECTION note on this bead; the earlier shape here crashed `vite dev` on boot):

  // vite.config.ts
  import { wallowStyles } from "@bc-solutions-coder/styles/vite";
  import { tanstackStart } from "@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite";
  import react from "@vitejs/plugin-react";
  import { nitro } from "nitro/vite";
  import { defineConfig } from "vite";

  export default defineConfig({
    // REQUIRED: `vite dev` binds 3000 when PORT is unset, which is wrong for
    // wallow-auth (3002) and minimal-app (3010) and times out their Playwright
    // webServer. Per-app default: 3010 | 3002 | 3000.
    server: { port: Number(process.env.PORT ?? <app default>) },
    plugins: [
      tanstackStart({
        router: { routeFileIgnorePattern: String.raw`\.(test|spec)\.(ts|tsx)$` },
      }),
      react(),
      nitro(),
      ...wallowStyles(),
    ],
  });

There is NO `vite: { installDevServerMiddleware: ... }` key. Setting it to true makes `vite dev` fail to boot alongside nitro() -- see the PLAN CORRECTION note. This is not the forbidden "reach for Vite+ / a Vite 7 pin / a hand-rolled host" path; those stay forbidden and are not needed.

Each app's __root.tsx imports its stylesheet FOR SIDE EFFECTS (`import "../styles.css";`) and emits NO stylesheet link from head(). The `?url` + head().links pattern ships a 404ing stylesheet in production -- see the PLAN CORRECTION note.

Version pins (@tanstack/react-start, @tanstack/react-router, @tanstack/react-router-ssr-query, nitro) are set per-app, in that app's own migration task, exact (no ^). Spike-validated set: @tanstack/react-start 1.168.32, @tanstack/react-router 1.170.18 (MUST match exactly -- react-start pins that exact version itself, so any other value installs two router copies), @tanstack/react-router-ssr-query 1.167.1, nitro 3.0.260610-beta (still the only dist-tag; pin exactly and re-run the 4.1 container checks on any bump). Each app also removes @tanstack/router-cli, tsr.config.json, routes:generate scripts (the Start plugin owns codegen now), and its direct h3 dependency.

