1. apps/wallow-auth/dev-server.ts:62-64 — add the fourth prefix to isProxyRequest:

     function isProxyRequest(pathname: string): boolean {
       return (
         pathname === '/health' ||
         pathname.startsWith('/v1/') ||
         pathname.startsWith('/connect/') ||
         pathname.startsWith('/.well-known/')
       );
     }

   apps/wallow-auth/server.ts already has exactly this predicate (landed in Wallow-vec7.5.1.1, with a comment explaining the /.well-known/ case). Mirror it verbatim so the two hosts stop diverging. Nothing else in dev-server.ts changes: handleProxy already lazily builds and memoises the AuthServer, and createAuthServer already mounts /.well-known/** — the ONLY thing missing is the gate letting those paths through.

2. NOTE ON ORDERING (matters, do not skip): the '/.well-known/' check must sit in isProxyRequest, i.e. BEFORE vite.middlewares. Vite owns paths under /.well-known in some setups; routing through the proxy first keeps the behaviour identical to server.ts and to production.

3. Test surface is honest but thin — dev-server.ts is a listening side effect from its first line and cannot be imported under test, and vitest only collects src/**/*.test.ts (vitest.config.ts). isProxyRequest is a module-private function in a non-collected file. Two options, implementer's call, state the choice on the bead:
