## Vulnerability (NEW-API-1, MEDIUM, Risk Score 9)

RealtimeHub.cs:16-31 OnConnectedAsync broadcasts a UserOnline event to tenant:{tenantId} group but never calls Groups.AddToGroupAsync(). Clients must manually call JoinGroup, creating a window of inconsistency and making tenant-scoped broadcasts non-functional for new connections.

## Files to Modify
- src/Foundry.Api/Hubs/RealtimeHub.cs (OnConnectedAsync method)

## Remediation
Add auto-join to tenant group:
```csharp
public override async Task OnConnectedAsync()
{
    Guid tenantId = _tenantContext.TenantId.Value;
    string userId = Context.UserIdentifier!;
    string tenantGroup = $"tenant:{tenantId}";

    await Groups.AddToGroupAsync(Context.ConnectionId, tenantGroup);
    await _presenceService.TrackConnectionAsync(tenantId, userId, Context.ConnectionId);
    await Clients.Group(tenantGroup).SendAsync("UserOnline", new { UserId = userId });
    await base.OnConnectedAsync();
}
```

## Testing
- Verify new connections automatically receive tenant-scoped broadcasts
- Verify UserOnline event reaches other tenant members
- Verify cross-tenant broadcasts are NOT received

