=== 7. RISKS / WHAT WOULD FALSIFY THIS DESIGN ===

- If a future fork or PR legitimately wants a module-specific flag that ISN'T meant to gate the whole module (e.g. a sub-feature toggle unrelated to enable/disable), naming it "Modules.X" for an X that isn't a real module name would now fail ModuleFeatureFlagTests. That's the intended behaviour (this is exactly the Modules.Configuration defect class), but a maintainer hitting this for a legitimate reason should rename the flag outside the "Modules." prefix rather than exempting it — flag this in code review if it comes up.
- The enforcement is CI-time only (a fork that edits appsettings.json and never runs the test suite could still ship drift) — consistent with every other architecture-test guarantee in this repo (e.g. ApiConventionTests), not a new class of risk.
- If IsCore is ever granted to a second module beyond Identity, ModuleFeatureFlagTests adapts automatically (reads `!module.IsCore` from the registry each run) — no hardcoded module list to update. This was deliberately designed in, verify it holds if you add a core module as a manual sanity check.
